 <!-- 5. PROOF -->
 <section class="sec">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">04</span> · The result I'm proudest of</span><span>Negative control</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">I tested whether it would refuse to guess.</h2><p class="rv d1">Same question, same company, run twice. The second time I deleted the evidence that explains the drop. <b>A tool that's guessing tells the same story both times. ORION didn't.</b></p></div>
  <figure class="vf rv" style="margin-top:44px">
   <span class="c tl"></span><span class="c tr"></span><span class="c bl"></span><span class="c br"></span>
   <div class="hd"><span>FIG. 01 · THE SAME QUESTION, TWICE</span><span>FROM ORION'S TEST SUITE</span></div>
   <div class="duo">
    <div class="brief"><div class="m">A · With the evidence</div><div class="q">Why did revenue decline in July?</div>
     <div class="r"><small>WHAT HAPPENED</small><div>Revenue fell <b>18%</b>, $500K → $410K.</div></div>
     <div class="r"><small>DRIVER</small><div><b>One customer</b>, 88.9% of the decline.</div></div>
     <div class="r"><small>EXPLANATION</small><div>Validated against records from the weeks before.</div></div>
     <div class="r"><small>CONFIDENCE</small><div class="mtr"><i><b style="width:82%"></b></i><span class="m" style="color:var(--ink)">Validated</span></div></div></div>
    <div class="brief"><div class="m or">B · Evidence removed</div><div class="q">Why did revenue decline in July?</div>
     <div class="r"><small>WHAT HAPPENED</small><div>Revenue fell <b>18%</b>, $500K → $410K.</div></div>
     <div class="r"><small>DRIVER</small><div><b>One customer</b>, 88.9% of the decline.</div></div>
     <div class="r"><small>EXPLANATION</small><div class="x">None stated. The evidence doesn't prove a cause.</div></div>
     <div class="r"><small>CONFIDENCE</small><div class="mtr"><i><b style="width:44%"></b></i><span class="m or">Capped · 0.44</span></div></div></div>
   </div>
  </figure>
  <div class="note rv"><div class="m">Engineering note</div><p>Testing also caught a real planner bug: the AI only searched for evidence <b>in the month revenue fell</b>, missing incidents from the weeks before. The validator now always reaches back a month, whatever the model plans, and a regression test replays the exact failing plan.</p></div>
 </section>

 <!-- 6. SIX CAPABILITIES -->
 <section class="sec">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">05</span> · The vision</span><span>Six capabilities</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">From answering questions to spotting problems first.</h2><p class="rv d1">Today, most AI assistants wait to be asked. The finished ORION connects, investigates, watches and helps people act, with <b>humans approving anything important</b>.</p></div>
  <div class="six">
   <div class="cp rv"><div class="h"><span class="n">A</span><span class="st">FOUNDATION BUILT</span></div><h4>Connect</h4><p>Link approved tools into one permission-aware map of documents, records, metrics and how they relate.</p><div class="ex">The point isn't collecting data. It's <b>connecting what lives apart</b>.</div></div>
   <div class="cp rv d1"><div class="h"><span class="n">B</span><span class="st b">BUILT</span></div><h4>Ask</h4><p>Ask hard business questions and get answers from the company's own evidence, with sources.</p><div class="ex">If the evidence isn't strong enough, <b>ORION says so</b>.</div></div>
   <div class="cp rv d2"><div class="h"><span class="n">C</span><span class="st b">BUILT</span></div><h4>Investigate</h4><p>Break a question into steps, pull evidence across departments, test explanations and report confidence.</p><div class="ex">Its biggest differentiator: <b>it investigates, not just responds</b>.</div></div>
   <div class="cp rv"><div class="h"><span class="n">D</span><span class="st f">PLANNED</span></div><h4>Monitor</h4><p>Watch approved sources for meaningful changes and flag risks before someone has to ask.</p>
    <div class="alert"><div class="t"><span>● RENEWAL RISK</span><span>ILLUSTRATIVE</span></div><b>Cedar Ridge · renewal at risk</b><p>Reporting delayed, export issues unresolved. Review with customer success.</p></div></div>
   <div class="cp rv d1"><div class="h"><span class="n">E</span><span class="st f">PLANNED</span></div><h4>Brief</h4><p>A short Monday-morning briefing: what changed, who needs attention, what's moving the wrong way, and the evidence for each.</p><div class="ex">Less time gathering. <b>More time deciding.</b></div></div>
   <div class="cp rv d2"><div class="h"><span class="n">F</span><span class="st f">PLANNED</span></div><h4>Act</h4><p>Propose the next step, like a Jira task or a customer follow-up, and run it only after explicit approval.</p><div class="ex">Not an AI that runs the business. <b>One that helps people act responsibly.</b></div></div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <!-- 7. ARCHITECTURE -->
 <section class="sec">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">06</span> · How it works</span><span>Target architecture</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">Built in layers, for decisions that cost money.</h2><p class="rv d1">Some layers are implemented and others are planned. Every layer follows the same principles, because a wrong business answer has real financial consequences.</p></div>
  <div class="arch">
   <div class="layers rv">
    <div class="ly"><span class="n">L1</span><div><h5>Connected business systems</h5><p>CRM · Documents · Projects · Support · Finance</p></div><span class="st f">PLANNED</span></div>
    <div class="ly"><span class="n">L2</span><div><h5>Ingestion &amp; sync</h5><p>Parsing · Normalization · Change detection · Permissions</p></div><span class="st">PARTIAL</span></div>
    <div class="ly core"><span class="n">L3</span><div><h5>Company knowledge layer</h5><p>PostgreSQL · pgvector · Documents · Metrics · Relationships</p></div><span class="st b">BUILT</span></div>
    <div class="ly core"><span class="n">L4</span><div><h5>Reasoning &amp; investigation engine</h5><p>Retrieval · Planning · Tool execution · Evidence validation</p></div><span class="st b">BUILT</span></div>
    <div class="surf"><div>Ask</div><div>Investigate</div><div>Insights · next</div></div>
   </div>
   <div class="prin rv d1"><div class="m" style="padding:0 0 14px;border:0;display:block">Design principles</div>
    <div><span>01</span>Isolate each company's data</div><div><span>02</span>Keep the source of every piece of evidence</div><div><span>03</span>Put hard limits on what the AI can do</div><div><span>04</span>Test the failure cases, not just the happy path</div><div><span>05</span>Make uncertainty visible</div></div>
  </div>
 </section>

